BEGIN_PGML Consider the function [`f(x) = e^x`] near [`a = 0\text{.}`] We know that [`f’(x) = e^x\text{,}`] so [`f’(0) = 1\text{;}`] along with the fact that [`f(0) = 1\text{,}`] it follows that the tangent line approximation is
[``` L(x) = f(0) + f’(0)(x-0) = 1 + 1(x - 0) = 1 + x \text{.}```]
Here is the function [`f(x) = e^x`] and its tangent line [`L(x) = 1 + x`] near the point [`(0, f(0))\text{.}`]
>> [@image(insertGraph($image_1), width=>600, alt=>qq"Graph of a function and its tangent line intersecting at a point and staying close near the point.")@]* <<
END_PGML
############################################################ # Scaffold ############################################################ Scaffold::Begin(numbered => 1,is_open => "correct_or_first_incorrect",can_open => always,);
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML Build a spreadsheet that computes the difference between [`f(x)`] and [`L(x)`] for [`x`]-values between [`-1`] and [`1\text{,}`] spaced [`0.1`] units apart. *Note:* we will revisit this spreadsheet for additional computations in Activity[$NBSP]*8.1.12, so it would be ideal if you save your work electronically in place you can find it later.
Your spreadsheet should start like the following table:
>> [@DataTable( [ [ [PGML('Row'), rowbottom => '1', midrule => '1',], PGML('[`\Delta x`]'), PGML('[`x`]'), PGML('[`f(x) = e^x`]'), PGML('[`L(x) = 1 + x`]'), ], [ [PGML('0'), rowbottom => '1', midrule => '1',], PGML('[`0.1`]'), PGML('[`-1.0`]'), PGML('[`0.36787\ldots`]'), PGML('[`0.0`]'), ], [ [PGML('1'), rowbottom => '1', midrule => '1',], PGML('[`0.1`]'), PGML('[`-0.9`]'), PGML('[`0.40656\ldots`]'), PGML('[`0.1`]'), ], [ [PGML('2'), rowbottom => '1', midrule => '1',], PGML('[`0.1`]'), PGML('[`-0.8`]'), PGML('[`0.44932\ldots`]'), PGML('[`0.2`]'), ], [ [PGML('⋮'), rowbottom => '1', midrule => '1',], PGML('⋮'), PGML('⋮'), PGML('⋮'), PGML('⋮'), ], ], align => '!{\vrule width 0.11em}c|c|c|c|c!{\vrule width 0.11em}', valign => 'middle', top => '3',);@]* <<
Then Row 14 is:
>> [@DataTable( [ [ [PGML('Row'), rowbottom => '1', midrule => '1',], PGML('[`\Delta x`]'), PGML('[`x`]'), PGML('[`f(x) = e^x`]'), PGML('[`L(x) = 1 + x`]'), ], [ [PGML('14'), rowbottom => '1', midrule => '1',], PGML('[_]{0.1}{3}'), PGML('[_]{0.4}{3}'), PGML('[_]{exp(0.4)}{3}'), PGML('[_]{1.4}{3}'), ], ], align => '!{\vrule width 0.11em}c|c|c|c|c!{\vrule width 0.11em}', valign => 'middle', top => '3',);@]* <<
END_PGML
